          <Textbox Name="Textbox2">
            <CanGrow>true</CanGrow>
            <KeepTogether>true</KeepTogether>
            <Paragraphs>
              <Paragraph>
                <TextRuns>
                  <TextRun>
                    <Value>We tested every wristband for 1530 chemicals. Overall, we detected  </Value>
                    <Style>
                      <FontStyle>Normal</FontStyle>
                      <FontFamily>Lato</FontFamily>
                      <FontSize>12pt</FontSize>
                      <FontWeight>Normal</FontWeight>
                      <TextDecoration>None</TextDecoration>
                    </Style>
                  </TextRun>
                  <TextRun>
                    <Value>=Fields!overall_detections.Value</Value>
                    <Style>
                      <FontStyle>Normal</FontStyle>
                      <FontFamily>Lato</FontFamily>
                      <FontSize>12pt</FontSize>
                      <FontWeight>Normal</FontWeight>
                      <TextDecoration>None</TextDecoration>
                    </Style>
                  </TextRun>
                  <TextRun>
                    <Value> chemicals. The full list of chemicals that we tested for is available online: </Value>
                    <Style>
                      <FontStyle>Normal</FontStyle>
                      <FontFamily>Lato</FontFamily>
                      <FontSize>12pt</FontSize>
                      <FontWeight>Normal</FontWeight>
                      <TextDecoration>None</TextDecoration>
                    </Style>
                  </TextRun>
                  <TextRun>
                    <Value>https://fses.oregonstate.edu/methods/1530</Value>
                    <ActionInfo>
                      <Actions>
                        <Action>
                          <Hyperlink>https://fses.oregonstate.edu/methods/1530</Hyperlink>
                        </Action>
                      </Actions>
                    </ActionInfo>
                    <MarkupType>HTML</MarkupType>
                    <Style>
                      <FontStyle>Normal</FontStyle>
                      <FontFamily>Lato</FontFamily>
                      <FontSize>12pt</FontSize>
                      <FontWeight>Normal</FontWeight>
                      <TextDecoration>None</TextDecoration>
                      <Color>DimGray</Color>
                    </Style>
                  </TextRun>
                </TextRuns>
                <Style>
                  <TextAlign>Left</TextAlign>
                </Style>
              </Paragraph>
              <Paragraph>
                <TextRuns>
                  <TextRun>
                    <Value />
                    <Style>
                      <FontStyle>Normal</FontStyle>
                      <FontFamily>Lato</FontFamily>
                      <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                      <FontWeight>Normal</FontWeight>
                      <TextDecoration>None</TextDecoration>
                    </Style>
                  </TextRun>
                </TextRuns>
                <Style>
                  <TextAlign>Left</TextAlign>
                </Style>
              </Paragraph>
              <Paragraph>
                <TextRuns>
                  <TextRun>
                    <Value>We are able to detect very low levels of chemicals. These numbers show the amount of chemical in the wristband. We use a unit of measurement called a mole. A “mole” is a way to measure how much of a chemical was found in the tag. This way of measuring lets us know the number of molecules found, instead of the weight of them. Think of it like a “dozen.” A dozen elephants weigh more than a dozen eggs, but there are twelve of each of them. A mole uses a similar concept, but lets us look at very small chemical concentrations.</Value>
                    <Style>
                      <FontStyle>Normal</FontStyle>
                      <FontFamily>Lato</FontFamily>
                      <FontSize>12pt</FontSize>
                      <FontWeight>Normal</FontWeight>
                      <TextDecoration>None</TextDecoration>
                    </Style>
                  </TextRun>
                </TextRuns>
                <Style>
                  <TextAlign>Left</TextAlign>
                </Style>
              </Paragraph>
              <Paragraph>
                <TextRuns>
                  <TextRun>
                    <Value />
                    <Style>
                      <FontStyle>Normal</FontStyle>
                      <FontFamily>Lato</FontFamily>
                      <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                      <FontWeight>Normal</FontWeight>
                      <TextDecoration>None</TextDecoration>
                    </Style>
                  </TextRun>
                </TextRuns>
                <Style>
                  <TextAlign>Left</TextAlign>
                </Style>
              </Paragraph>
              <Paragraph>
                <TextRuns>
                  <TextRun>
                    <Value>This table shows the name of each chemical, organized by chemical classification. The table shows how many times a chemical was found. For example, if a chemical was found </Value>
                    <Style>
                      <FontStyle>Normal</FontStyle>
                      <FontFamily>Lato</FontFamily>
                      <FontSize>12pt</FontSize>
                      <FontWeight>Normal</FontWeight>
                      <TextDecoration>None</TextDecoration>
                    </Style>
                  </TextRun>
                  <TextRun>
                    <Value>=Fields!total_participants.Value</Value>
                    <Style>
                      <FontStyle>Normal</FontStyle>
                      <FontFamily>Lato</FontFamily>
                      <FontSize>12pt</FontSize>
                      <FontWeight>Normal</FontWeight>
                      <TextDecoration>None</TextDecoration>
                    </Style>
                  </TextRun>
                  <TextRun>
                    <Value> times, it was found in every wristband in the study. The amount in your wristband is shown on the right.</Value>
                    <Style>
                      <FontStyle>Normal</FontStyle>
                      <FontFamily>Lato</FontFamily>
                      <FontSize>12pt</FontSize>
                      <FontWeight>Normal</FontWeight>
                      <TextDecoration>None</TextDecoration>
                    </Style>
                  </TextRun>
                </TextRuns>
                <Style>
                  <TextAlign>Left</TextAlign>
                </Style>
              </Paragraph>
            </Paragraphs>
